                <pb facs="0819" n="795" xml:id="pg795"/>

                <head>Meeting of United States Ambassadors at Rome, March 22–24, 1950</head>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </p>
                <p>At the end of the meeting of the United States Ambassadors in London at the end
                    of October 1949, the participants expressed the feeling that periodic
                    conferences should be arranged for similar exchanges of views and reports on the
                    situation in Western Europe. With this in mind during the first two months of
                    1950 communications were exchanged between Washington, Rome, London, Paris,
                    Moscow, and Frankfort to decide on the site and agenda for the next Ambassadors’
                    meeting. Documentation on these preparations is in file 120.43/1–3150 ff. For
                    documentation on the 1949 meeting in Paris, see <ref
                        target="frus:frus1949v04/pg_469">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1949, volume IV, pages
                        469</ref> ff.</p>



